      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T21:56:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`CFStringTokenizer` operates in utf16 space, right?  I think we need to convert the range back to utf8 byte offsets.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "1aa337c49a1cab965512435835507b9a4105021b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ee733c5_7b363de7",
        "filename": "modules/skunicode/src/SkUnicode_apple.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 8956
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T22:34:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right. CFStringTokenizer returns UTF-16 offsets, which violates the UTF-8 byte contract of SkBreakIterator. Addressed in follow-up CL 1388876 by building a UTF-16 to UTF-8 offset mapping (u16ToU8).\nThis method is not used by Flutter.",
      "parentUuid": "d950b457_7283db64",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "1aa337c49a1cab965512435835507b9a4105021b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed2d7a72_139192cb",
        "filename": "modules/skunicode/src/SkUnicode_apple.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T21:56:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is `CFStringCreateWithBytesNoCopy` performs strict utf8 validation, and returns nullptr if there are illegal sequences.  Since we bail in that case, I\u0027m not sure this fallback code is reachable.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 126,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "1aa337c49a1cab965512435835507b9a4105021b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5ceadc8_c149f3e1",
        "filename": "modules/skunicode/src/SkUnicode_apple.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 8956
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T22:34:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CFStringCreateWithBytesNoCopy strictly validates UTF-8 and bails out earlier if invalid. Removed the dead fallback code.",
      "parentUuid": "ed2d7a72_139192cb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 126,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "1aa337c49a1cab965512435835507b9a4105021b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed67b555_115e4ff1",
        "filename": "modules/skunicode/src/SkUnicode_apple.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T21:56:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So if `CFStringTokenizer` did not emit a soft break for `pos16`, we\u0027re appending it here - but that means it could be out of order relative to the other breaks.  Shouldn\u0027t we insert it such that the breaks remain sorted?",
      "revId": "1aa337c49a1cab965512435835507b9a4105021b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89ee3761_72c561a4",
        "filename": "modules/skunicode/src/SkUnicode_apple.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 8956
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T22:34:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Handled in follow-up CL 1388876 using binary-search sorted insertion (std::lower_bound) to guarantee strictly monotonically increasing breaks.",
      "parentUuid": "ed67b555_115e4ff1",
      "revId": "1aa337c49a1cab965512435835507b9a4105021b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "afc41543_4077d2e7",
        "filename": "modules/skunicode/src/SkUnicode_apple.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 176,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T21:56:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure about the expected semantics for this entry point: are the resulting break offsets expected to be UTF-16 or UTF-8?  If the former, we may not be able to call into the utf8 version here.",
      "revId": "1aa337c49a1cab965512435835507b9a4105021b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c1f57e7_eb0d575e",
        "filename": "modules/skunicode/src/SkUnicode_apple.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 176,
      "author": {
        "id": 8956
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T22:34:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The contract expects UTF-16 offsets for char16_t input. Addressed in follow-up CL 1388876: setText(char16_t) now operates directly in UTF-16 space via CFStringCreateWithCharactersNoCopy without round-tripping to UTF-8.",
      "parentUuid": "afc41543_4077d2e7",
      "revId": "1aa337c49a1cab965512435835507b9a4105021b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ca91383_6e4f2679",
        "filename": "modules/skunicode/src/SkUnicode_apple.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 422,
